---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  slug="contributor-workflow"
  title="ML Contributor Workflow | MIAR Documentation"
  description="Safe multi-contributor workflow for configuring DVC, pulling training data, publishing corpus revisions, and releasing MIAR model packages."
>
  <section id="identity">
    <h2>Every contributor uses an individual identity</h2>
    <p>
      Each person or automation receives separate, bucket-scoped R2 credentials with only the
      object permissions required for its role. Administrator tokens are never shared. Credentials
      stay in the contributor's local environment or approved secret manager and never enter Git,
      documentation, issue comments, model evidence, or chat transcripts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare documents how to create
      <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/api/tokens/" rel="external">R2 API tokens</a>
      and how those credentials are used through the
      <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/get-started/s3/" rel="external">S3-compatible endpoint</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="bootstrap">
    <h2>Bootstrap the local ML workspace</h2>
    <ol class="docs-steps">
      <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Clone safely</strong><p>Create a feature branch or assigned worktree. Never rewrite shared history or work directly on a teammate's branch.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Install the locked environment</strong><p>Use the repository setup target so DVC, MLflow clients, training dependencies, and verification tools match the project.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Configure local credentials</strong><p>Store scoped R2 keys outside Git and configure the DVC remote locally.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Verify before transfer</strong><p>Run the remote health check, then pull only the corpus revision required by the assigned work.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>make setup-mlops-venv
make dataset-remote-configure
make dataset-remote-health
make dataset-pull</code></pre>
    <p>
      Target names describe the MIAR repository contract. Consult the repository's
      <code>Makefile</code> and contributor guide for environment-specific prerequisites.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="dataset-change">
    <h2>Publish a dataset change</h2>
    <ol class="docs-steps">
      <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Validate rights and lineage</strong><p>Confirm source terms, provenance, metadata completeness, and permitted use before adding imagery.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Run corpus validation</strong><p>Check labels, ontology compatibility, checksums, duplicate scenes, and split leakage.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Create the DVC revision</strong><p>Track the reviewed corpus and push its binary objects to R2.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Review the pointer</strong><p>Commit only the DVC pointer, manifest, policy changes, and intentional code changes to Git.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>dvc add path/to/corpus
make dataset-push
git add path/to/corpus.dvc path/to/manifest.json
make ci-local</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="model-change">
    <h2>Publish a model candidate</h2>
    <ul class="docs-checklist">
      <li>Log the governed training and benchmark runs to MLflow.</li>
      <li>Build the complete evidence bundle described in the <a href="/docs/model-packages/">model package contract</a>.</li>
      <li>Verify all checksums and ensure the package references an existing Git and DVC revision.</li>
      <li>Push the immutable candidate bundle to the model-release prefix in R2.</li>
      <li>Request promotion through the MIAR registry. Uploading a package does not approve it.</li>
    </ul>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>make model-bundle-verify
make model-push-r2
make ci-local</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="review">
    <h2>Review gate</h2>
    <div class="docs-state-grid docs-state-grid-compact">
      <article><span>Data</span><p>Rights, lineage, checksums, ontology, and split integrity are recorded.</p></article>
      <article><span>Evidence</span><p>Run identity, benchmark metrics, limitations, and failure analysis are complete.</p></article>
      <article><span>Security</span><p>No credentials, restricted paths, or sensitive source details appear in Git or logs.</p></article>
      <article><span>Release</span><p>The package verifies, local CI passes, and approval remains separate from publication.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="safety">
    <h2>Git and credential safety</h2>
    <ul class="docs-checklist">
      <li>Pull and inspect divergence before starting; isolate work in a branch or worktree.</li>
      <li>Do not force-push, rewrite shared history, or rebase a branch used by another contributor.</li>
      <li>Do not commit generated corpora, weights, caches, local databases, or environment files.</li>
      <li>Run <code>make ci-local</code> before every push and publish only intentional, reviewable commits.</li>
      <li>Rotate any secret immediately if it is exposed outside the approved secret boundary.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>See the official <a href="https://git-scm.com/doc" rel="external">Git documentation</a> for command reference.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
